Mario Party 4 -- the M1 PowerPC binary on the real Power Mac G4
===============================================================

Captured 2026-09-13 on the G4 test bench: Power Mac G4, Mac OS X 10.5.4 (9E25),
Radeon 9000, big endian.  Binary: port/build-ppc-darwin/marioparty4 built by
port/build-ppc.sh (powerpc-apple-darwin8 GCC 14.2, MacOSX10.4u SDK,
-malign-natural -mone-byte-bool), wrapped by port/tools/make_bundle.sh and
installed by port/tools/g4_install.sh as ~/MarioParty4.app.  Disc image:
~/MarioParty4/mp4.nkit.iso, the same 598,382,592-byte NKit ISO as on the host.

    ./MarioParty4.app/Contents/MacOS/isle --watchdog 6

Boot from `main()` to the REL seam takes under a second; the rest of the run is
the documented spin in omWatchOverlayProc, which the watchdog ends.  What
differs from docs/m1-boot.log (the same build on the little-endian development
host) is listed at the bottom of this file.

